# The real domain. Anything still pointing at the old Netlify address —
# bookmarks, installed PWAs, mails already sent, the Play listing until it is
# updated — lands on the same path on covertcook.fr. `!` forces it even where a
# file exists at that path. Above the SPA fallback, which would otherwise
# answer first.
https://covertcook.netlify.app/*  https://covertcook.fr/:splat  301!
https://www.covertcook.fr/*       https://covertcook.fr/:splat  301!

# Icons moved into folders (public/ reorganised). Old URLs live on in emails
# already sent, in the Play listing and in installed PWAs' cached manifests.
# Above the SPA fallback: Netlify takes the first rule that matches, and these
# files no longer exist, so below it they were answered with index.html — an
# HTML page where a mail client expected the logo, i.e. a broken image.
/pwa-192x192.png          /pwa/pwa-192x192.png          301
/pwa-512x512.png          /pwa/pwa-512x512.png          301
/pwa-maskable-512x512.png /pwa/pwa-512x512.png 301
/favicon-32.png           /favicons/favicon-32.png      301
/favicon-192.png          /favicons/favicon-192.png     301
/apple-touch-icon.png     /favicons/apple-touch-icon.png 301

# Everything else is a client-side route. Last, so it never shadows a rule above.
/*    /index.html   200
